<title>NETHERLANDS: UNI-INVEST Q1 PROFIT UP 25 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>UNI-INVEST Q1 PROFIT UP 25 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter of 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>Net profit (direct inv result)  15.3  vs 12.2</p>
<p>Total investment result</p>
<p>    after property revaluations     29.93 vs 23.31</p>
<p>    Net per share  direct(guilders)  0.62 vs  0.61</p>
<p>    Ditto indirect			 0.14 vs  0.56</p>
<p>    Total investment income	   11.22 vs  9.92</p>
<p>    Operating costs			3.41 vs  2.58</p>
<p>    Tax					1.0  vs  18.0</p>
<p>    Extraordinary income		 nil  vs  1.35</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the property fund is Uni-Invest NV.</p>
<p>Uni-Invest said it expected 1997 direct investment</p>
<p>result per share to be some six percent above 1996's.</p>
<p>In March, it had said it expected 1997 total investment</p>
<p>result per share to rise over five percent compared to 1996.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
